WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.375
PRIYANKA VERGADIA:
Do you find it

00:00:01.375 --> 00:00:02.880
challenging to
maintain identities

00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:05.700
across different environments
and hybrid and multi-cloud

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:06.960
deployments?

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:09.570
Do you wish you can leverage
your existing identity

00:00:09.570 --> 00:00:11.490
investments for Anthos?

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:13.260
Well, keep watching
as we cover how

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:17.250
you can use Anthos to simplify
identity management for users

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:18.090
and workloads.

00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:20.460
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:24.080
Hi.

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:27.650
I'm Priyanka Vergadia, and
welcome to "Anthos 101."

00:00:27.650 --> 00:00:30.500
With Anthos, our goal
is to make it seamless

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:33.170
for you to modernize and
manage your workloads

00:00:33.170 --> 00:00:35.450
in an environment
that you prefer,

00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:38.390
whether it is on-prem,
Google Cloud, Edge,

00:00:38.390 --> 00:00:40.400
or a different cloud.

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:42.950
Anthos spans across
multiple environments,

00:00:42.950 --> 00:00:46.970
and each is built on different
identity store, for example,

00:00:46.970 --> 00:00:50.270
Active Directory for on-prem,
Cloud Identity for Google

00:00:50.270 --> 00:00:53.120
Cloud, and AWS IAM for AWS.

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:55.190
In addition to
employee identity,

00:00:55.190 --> 00:00:59.030
you may need to manage partner,
[INAUDIBLE] identity, workload

00:00:59.030 --> 00:01:02.870
identity, or customer
identity, further increasing

00:01:02.870 --> 00:01:04.010
the complexity.

00:01:04.010 --> 00:01:06.560
Traditionally, Google
Cloud has offered

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:09.440
a synchronization-based
identity model,

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:13.070
requiring you to synchronize
identities with Google Cloud.

00:01:13.070 --> 00:01:15.240
While this may work
for certain scenarios,

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:18.830
you may have concerns around
consistency and latency

00:01:18.830 --> 00:01:22.190
for a hybrid or
multi-cloud deployment.

00:01:22.190 --> 00:01:24.830
With Anthos, we want to
meet you where you are.

00:01:24.830 --> 00:01:28.340
Anthos Identity Service
extends existing capabilities

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:31.700
and it enables you to use
third-party identity providers

00:01:31.700 --> 00:01:35.510
and authentication protocols,
following a federation model.

00:01:35.510 --> 00:01:38.780
This service can be deployed
quickly in your Anthos GKE

00:01:38.780 --> 00:01:42.530
cluster, enabling protocols
such as OpenID Connect.

00:01:42.530 --> 00:01:44.960
You no longer need to
synchronize identities

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:47.630
to Google Cloud or
worry about consistency

00:01:47.630 --> 00:01:49.190
across environments.

00:01:49.190 --> 00:01:51.410
It saves time and
reduces friction

00:01:51.410 --> 00:01:54.510
during the onboarding process.

00:01:54.510 --> 00:01:57.400
Anthos on-prem
offers OIDC support,

00:01:57.400 --> 00:02:00.120
which enables
authentication via G Cloud

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:01.830
or through Cloud Console.

00:02:01.830 --> 00:02:04.800
Let's walk through how
that experience looks like.

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:07.680
Say you are a platform
administrator managing

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:09.930
a small team of
developers, and you're

00:02:09.930 --> 00:02:13.860
interested in providing access
to the Kubernetes API server

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:17.160
to debug issues or perform
cluster management tasks

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:19.140
using Kubectl.

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:22.500
After creating a user
cluster for GKE on-prem,

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:26.940
you can run a gkectl command to
generate a login configuration

00:02:26.940 --> 00:02:27.620
file.

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:29.970
You will need to populate
this file with values

00:02:29.970 --> 00:02:32.010
specific to your
identity provider,

00:02:32.010 --> 00:02:36.300
such as issuer URL,
redirect URL, and client ID.

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:39.960
You can enable one or multiple
identity providers to support

00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:42.330
needs of different user groups.

00:02:42.330 --> 00:02:45.360
The file can be securely
distributed to developers

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:47.550
using an accessible URL.

00:02:47.550 --> 00:02:51.120
In order to restrict access
based on privileges granted

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:53.490
to authenticated
users, you can use

00:02:53.490 --> 00:02:56.040
Kubernetes role-based
access control

00:02:56.040 --> 00:02:59.580
to create cluster roles that
grant specific privileges

00:02:59.580 --> 00:03:01.590
to users and groups.

00:03:01.590 --> 00:03:04.680
As a developer, you can
install the G Cloud SDK

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:07.890
without requiring a Google
Cloud Identity account

00:03:07.890 --> 00:03:10.590
and install the Anthos
autho components

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:13.950
to enable third-party
OIDC authentication.

00:03:13.950 --> 00:03:16.740
Simply run gcloud
anthos auth login,

00:03:16.740 --> 00:03:19.200
to view the list of
available clusters

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:22.110
and specify a cluster
flag to log in.

00:03:22.110 --> 00:03:24.850
Based on your Kubernetes
RBAC privileges,

00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:27.870
you can now run Kubectl
commands to complete

00:03:27.870 --> 00:03:31.020
your required tasks.

00:03:31.020 --> 00:03:34.350
Moving forward, we are planning
to enable additional protocols,

00:03:34.350 --> 00:03:37.170
such as LDAP, to support
authentication needs

00:03:37.170 --> 00:03:39.960
for multiple environments,
including Google Cloud,

00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:42.090
on-prem, and other clouds.

00:03:42.090 --> 00:03:45.750
We're also extending our OIDC
capabilities to other clouds

00:03:45.750 --> 00:03:49.080
to create a consistent
multi-cloud experience.

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:52.410
Anthos Identity Service is
designed to work seamlessly

00:03:52.410 --> 00:03:55.710
with other Anthos components
and your existing identity

00:03:55.710 --> 00:03:57.570
investments.

00:03:57.570 --> 00:03:59.910
Beyond user authentication,
you can also

00:03:59.910 --> 00:04:02.790
enable workload
authentication for workloads

00:04:02.790 --> 00:04:05.670
running in GKE to
consume services

00:04:05.670 --> 00:04:07.710
provided by Google APIs.

00:04:07.710 --> 00:04:10.380
Simply configure a
Kubernetes service account

00:04:10.380 --> 00:04:12.240
to automatically
authenticate when

00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:14.380
accessing Google Cloud APIs.

00:04:14.380 --> 00:04:16.500
There's no need to
worry about safeguarding

00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:20.820
private keys for PKI and client
certificates or managing bearer

00:04:20.820 --> 00:04:22.470
and bootstrap tokens.

00:04:22.470 --> 00:04:25.800
Anthos Identity Service
provides a fully integrated,

00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:28.710
enterprise-ready solution
for authentication that

00:04:28.710 --> 00:04:31.050
is built with security in mind.

00:04:31.050 --> 00:04:33.660
As you can see, Anthos
Identity Service

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:36.870
offers a seamless solution
for managing authentication

00:04:36.870 --> 00:04:39.600
to multiple Anthos
GKE environments,

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:43.050
allowing you to leverage
existing identity investments

00:04:43.050 --> 00:04:45.600
and streamline the
onboarding process.

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:47.820
To learn more about
Anthos Identity

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:51.030
Service and our identity
features, check out

00:04:51.030 --> 00:04:52.750
the documentation below.

00:04:52.750 --> 00:04:54.450
And for more Anthos
content, don't

00:04:54.450 --> 00:04:57.660
forget to subscribe and follow
the "Anthos 101" playlist.

00:04:57.660 --> 00:05:00.410
[MUSIC PLAYING]

